第二条 许可的范围

a. License grant.

a. 许可授予。

    1. Subject to the terms and conditions of this Public License, the Licensor hereby grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-sublicensable, non-exclusive, irrevocable license to exercise the Licensed Rights in the Licensed Material to:

    1. 根据本公共许可协议的条款和条件，许可人特此授予您在全球范围内、免许可费、不可再许可、非独占、不可撤销的许可，以对授权作品（Licensed Material）行使许可的权利（Licensed Rights）：

        A. reproduce and Share the Licensed Material, in whole or in part, for NonCommercial purposes only; and

        A. 全部或部分地复制和分享授权作品（Licensed Material），但仅限于非商业性目的；以及

        B. produce, reproduce, and Share Adapted Material for NonCommercial purposes only.

        B. 仅为非商业性目的，创作、复制和分享演绎作品（Adapted Material）。

    2. Exceptions and Limitations. For the avoidance of doubt, where Exceptions and Limitations apply to Your use, this Public License does not apply, and You do not need to comply with its terms and conditions.

    2. 例外与限制。为免疑义，如果例外与限制适用于您对授权作品（Licensed Material）的使用，本公共许可协议将不适用，您也无需遵守其条款和条件。

    3. Term. The term of this Public License is specified in Section 6(a).

    3. 期限。本公共许可协议的期限规定于第六条(a)款。

    4. Media and formats; technical modifications allowed. The Licensor authorizes You to exercise the Licensed Rights in all media and formats whether now known or hereafter created, and to make technical modifications necessary to do so. The Licensor waives and/or agrees not to assert any right or authority to forbid You from making technical modifications necessary to exercise the Licensed Rights, including technical modifications necessary to circumvent Effective Technological Measures. For purposes of this Public License, simply making modifications authorized by this Section 2(a)(4) never produces Adapted Material.

    4. 媒介和形式；允许的技术修改。许可人授权您在任何媒介和形式，不论现在已知或将来创制，行使本协议所许可的权利，并对此进行必要的技术修改。许可人放弃和/或同意不主张任何权利以禁止您为了行使本协议所许可的权利而进行必要的技术修改，包括为了规避有效的技术措施（Effective Technological Measures）所必需的技术修改。为本公共许可协议之目的，进行本条(a)款(4)项所授权的修改不构成演绎作品（Adapted Material）。

    5. Downstream recipients.

    5. 后续接受方。

        A. Offer from the Licensor – Licensed Material. Every recipient of the Licensed Material automatically receives an offer from the Licensor to exercise the Licensed Rights under the terms and conditions of this Public License.

        A. 来自许可人的要约——授权作品（Licensed Material）。授权作品（Licensed Material）的每一后续接受方自动获得许可人的要约，依据本公共许可协议的条款行使许可的权利（Licensed Rights）。

        B. Additional offer from the Licensor – Adapted Material. Every recipient of Adapted Material from You automatically receives an offer from the Licensor to exercise the Licensed Rights in the Adapted Material under the conditions of the Adapter's License You apply.

        B. 来自许可人的额外要约——演绎作品（Adapted Material）。您所创作的每一演绎作品（Adapted Material）的后续接受方自动获得许可人的要约，依据您所适用的演绎作者的许可（Adapter's License）的条款行使您在该演绎作品（Adapted Material）中所贡献的部分的许可的权利（Licensed Rights）。

        C. No downstream restrictions. You may not offer or impose any additional or different terms or conditions on, or apply any Effective Technological Measures to, the Licensed Material if doing so restricts exercise of the Licensed Rights by any recipient of the Licensed Material.

        C. 禁止对下游接收方设置限制。您不得就授权作品（Licensed Material）提出或增加任何额外或不同的条款或条件，或适用任何有效的技术措施（Effective Technological Measures），从而限制后续接收方行使许可的权利（Licensed Rights）。

    6. No endorsement. Nothing in this Public License constitutes or may be construed as permission to assert or imply that You are, or that Your use of the Licensed Material is, connected with, or sponsored, endorsed, or granted official status by, the Licensor or others designated to receive attribution as provided in Section 3(a)(1)(A)(i).

    6. 非背认。本公共许可协议中的任何内容均不构成或可被解释为允许您主张或暗示您或您对授权作品（Licensed Material）的使用与许可人或被指定为署名对象的第三方（如第三条(a)款(1)项(A)目(i)所规定）有关联、获得其赞助、认可或正式地位。

b. Other rights.

b. 其他权利。

    1. Moral rights, such as the right of integrity, are not licensed under this Public License, nor are publicity, privacy, and/or other similar personality rights; however, to the extent possible, the Licensor waives and/or agrees not to assert any such rights held by the Licensor to the limited extent necessary to allow You to exercise the Licensed Rights, but not otherwise.

    1. 精神权利，如保护作品完整权，以及形象权、隐私权和/或其他类似人格权利，不受本公共许可协议许可；但在可能的情况下，许可人放弃和/或同意在必要的限度内不主张其拥有的任何此类权利，以使您能够行使许可的权利，但不超出此限度。

    2. Patent and trademark rights are not licensed under this Public License.

    2. 专利权和商标权不受本公共许可协议许可。

    3. To the extent possible, the Licensor waives any right to collect royalties from You for the exercise of the Licensed Rights, whether directly or through a collecting society under any voluntary or waivable statutory or compulsory licensing scheme. In all other cases the Licensor expressly reserves any right to collect such royalties, including when the Licensed Material is used other than for NonCommercial purposes.

